The Karotz's internal USB hub says it is bus-powered, and 6.1 rejected the
Wi-Fi dongle and the USB key behind it ("rejected 1 configuration due to
insufficient available bus power", Gengar, 2026-11-24): the board powers
them itself, as 2.6.32 assumed. On RABBITV3 a configuration is not ruled
out for the current it draws.
--- a/drivers/usb/core/generic.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/core/generic.c
@@ -113,7 +113,8 @@ int usb_choose_configuration(struct usb_device *udev)
 		 */
 
 		/* Rule out configs that draw too much bus current */
-		if (usb_get_max_power(udev, c) > udev->bus_mA) {
+		if (usb_get_max_power(udev, c) > udev->bus_mA &&
+		    !IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_MACH_RABBITV3)) {
 			insufficient_power++;
 			continue;
 		}
